<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Práxedes Mateo Sagasta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1825">1825</a>–<a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Práxedes Mateo Sagasta was a Spanish politician and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> Restoration. He served as prime minister seven times between 1870 and 1902, alternating in power with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-canovas-del-castillo">Antonio Cánovas del Castillo</a>'s Conservatives under the turno pacífico. His governments introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-suffrage">universal male suffrage</a> in 1890, and he was in office during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a> of 1898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/praxedes-mateo-sagasta.jpg" alt="Práxedes Mateo Sagasta" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: Christian Franzen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pr%C3%A1xedes_Mateo_Sagasta_por_Christian_Franzen_(edit).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
